  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to exert its biological effects through a shared pathway involving flavopiridol and RET proto-oncogene. The evidence suggests that Oblonganoside C targets multiple entities, including Cytochrome P450 2E1 and LIM domain kinase 2, which are both targets of flavopiridol. Since flavopiridol is known to inhibit RET proto-oncogene, this implies that Oblonganoside C may modulate RET through a downstream effect on these intermediate targets. The high scores in all three paths indicate a consistent and significant relationship, though the exact mechanism of how Oblonganoside C influences RET remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of a common downstream target (RET) across different pathways supports a potential role for Oblonganoside C in regulating RET through a complex network of molecular interactions.",
